# ---- pending: select items under LIMIT (ADR 0041; roadmap PR SQ5b removes these guards) ----

# Without ORDER BY the LIMIT keeps two rows, and both engines compute the items only for those (DuckDB at one thread,
# as the runner runs it), so the casts that would fail for later cities are never computed. Which rows a LIMIT without
# ORDER BY keeps depends on the plan (the outer side's order through the join back), hence rowsort. With ORDER BY
# every row's item is computed, and both engines fail.
